---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About SignLingo"
	description="Learn ASL fingerspelling with real-time feedback"
	pubDate={new Date('January 28 2025')}
>
	<p>
		SignLingo is an open-source desktop application that teaches American Sign Language (ASL)
		fingerspelling through interactive, gamified lessons. Think Duolingo, but for hand signs.
	</p>

	<h2>How It Works</h2>
	<p>
		Using your webcam, SignLingo detects your hand position in real-time using MediaPipe's
		hand landmark detection. A lightweight TensorFlow.js model (just ~115KB) runs entirely
		in your browser to recognize which letter you're signing.
	</p>

	<p>
		The app guides you through progressive lessons, starting with simple letters and building
		up to full words and phrases. You get instant feedback on your signing accuracy.
	</p>

	<h2>Privacy First</h2>
	<p>
		All processing happens locally on your device. Your webcam feed never leaves your computer.
		No accounts, no cloud, no tracking.
	</p>

	<h2>Open Source</h2>
	<p>
		SignLingo is fully open source. Check out the code on
		<a href="https://github.com/ethanfalik/hand-sign">GitHub</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Tech Stack</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Electron + React + TypeScript</li>
		<li>MediaPipe Hands for landmark detection</li>
		<li>TensorFlow.js for in-browser ML</li>
		<li>Vite for development</li>
	</ul>
</Layout>
